[Music]  they are some of the most distressing  images of the invasion of the capitol  building  bloodied police officer daniel hodges  screaming out in pain  and begging for help recounting for the  first time what happened  he says he thought he wouldn't survive  someone managed to get his thumb in my  eye  my right eye and start gouging it out  thankfully i was able to shake him but  that was the second time where i'm  afraid of  you know that might be the end or i  might be maliciously disfigured  the footage of the chaos is still being  studied by investigators  and the intent of this mob is chilling  you know one of my ammunition magazines  was stripped from my belt  and guys were trying to grab my gun and  they were chanting like kill him with  his own gun  i could shoot him um  they're trying to kill me and i'm  justified  but if i did that i would provide them  with the justification that they  needed to kill me  but as some police officers are lauded  for their heroism  others are being investigated it's  thought some had a role in the chaos  the wider investigation is also  gathering pace  so far nearly 100 arrests  the authorities though are still trying  to identify more suspects  including the man wanted in connection  with the murder of police officer  brian sicknick and it's feared there  could be more attacks  in the days leading up to the  inauguration of president-elect  joe biden thousands of national guard  troops are fanned out across the capital  fortifying institutions we cannot allow  a recurrence  of the chaos in illegal activity that  the united states and the world  witnessed  last week  the storming of congress will go down as  one of the most dramatic security  breaches  in american history but along with the  failings there is also a story of  heroism  of those who stood their ground and  risked their lives  alex rossi sky news washington

